  "notes": [
    "In-process evidence is Layer A (this host) and is NOT Linux CI evidence.",
    "The cold arm empties the decoded card-text cache before each iteration; the OS page cache stays warm, so it measures the product cold path, not a disk-cold boot.",
    "ns/op on a shared 2-core host is noisy (the 10,000-card baseline arm ranged 4.96-9.13 s); every round is reported and the claim rests on the non-overlap of the two subjects, not on one median.",
    "bytes/op and allocs/op are deterministic for the same input bytes, so their tiny spread is measurement rounding, not host noise."
  ]
